{
  "explanation": "The attacker utilized the automated tool sqlmap from IP 198.51.100.12 to perform SQL injection attacks against various application endpoints, attempting UNION-based data extraction, authentication bypasses, table drops, and time-based blind injections. The HTTP status codes (400, 500, and 200) suggest that while some queries were blocked or resulted in server errors, others may have been successfully processed by the backend database.",
  "mitre_tactic": "Initial Access",
  "recommended_actions": [
    "Implement parameterized queries and prepared statements across all database interactions to neutralize SQL injection vectors.",
    "Block the source IP address 198.51.100.12 at the web application firewall (WAF) and perimeter firewall.",
    "Deploy input validation and sanitization filters to reject requests originating from known vulnerability scanners like sqlmap."
  ]
}
